WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.880
Nail detachment was over four times more common in people using glp-1 drugs. This is Peptides Weekly Episode 3. Education and evidence. Never dosing advice. Medical Express carried that report on September 30th. It calls the work the first controlled study of the comparison. A controlled human study can show a gap between groups. It does not tell you why one person's nail lifted. These are Peptide medicines listeners already hear about, so a harm signal sits

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:31.920
its beside the glucose and weight claims.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.720
In a new trial result, rather than another pass at weight loss

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:38.580
totals, Reuters says a Regeneron drug

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.680
halved muscle loss when it was combined

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:42.540
with Novo's semi-glutide.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:46.600
That finding is from a human trial reported September 30.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:50.260
Medical Express names the drug Trivogramab

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:54.540
and calls it anti-myostatin, meaning it blocks myostatin.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:57.880
The same report says lean mass can be preserved

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:00.540
during semi-glutide weight loss and after it.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:03.740
Muscle loss and scale weight are different measurements.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:07.460
Nothing in these reports states an approval for Travogramab.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:13.380
After earlier work on blood vessel markers, nature medicine put a randomized trial online

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:14.900
on October 1st.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:17.320
The people in it had type 2 diabetes.

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:20.900
The question was how semi-glutide might protect the kidney.

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:26.420
The notice names histology, multi-parametric MRI, and transcriptomics.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:29.480
That is a randomized human mechanism study.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:33.560
It is not, on this notice, account of who reached kidney failure.

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:36.420
A path is not the same thing as an outcome.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:43.840
The Lancet's post from EASD 2026 says Mauritius is the first country to show diabetes prevalence

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:48.200
falling over time, and intermediate hyperglycemia falling with it.

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:51.400
The measure was the oral glucose tolerance test.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:56.760
Next, the criteria WHO recommends, which the post calls the objective gold standard.

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:00.560
More sits in the Lancet Diabetes and Endocrinology.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:06.600
This is population surveillance, not a peptide trial, and it does not show that a drug caused

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:06.980
the drop.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:12.620
Eric Topel pointed to a nature paper from PushMeat and colleagues at Google DeepMind.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:18.440
They watermark AI-generated proteins and keep the proteins function, so someone can later

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:20.080
tell where a design came from.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:23.660
A Nature News piece runs beside the research article.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:29.420
This is a method's paper about designed proteins, not a human medicine trial, and it does

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:31.560
not show safety or benefit in people.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:35.180
Sleep disorders affect more than 70 million people.

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:41.260
A 2026 review in brain says, and that number is the doorway into this week's spotlight

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.120
on how to read peptide evidence.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:47.060
The review is not selling a sleep drug, it is showing a ladder.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:53.340
Optogenetics and chemogenetics can control sleep wake switches in animal models, so sleep

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:56.220
can be pushed around in those animals by hitting a circuit.

00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:01.420
The same review says moving that control into people faces substantial challenges.

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:04.540
Some principles look conserved across species.

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:11.120
Circuit layout, the tools we can actually use, and regulatory limits still differ, so human

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:12.580
work needs its own designs.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.920
A clean animal switch is not a human result.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:18.680
world. Read the rung before you trust the adjective.

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:24.680
A cell study asks whether a pathway can fire in a dish. An animal study asks whether

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:29.960
it matters in a living non-human body under controlled conditions. A small human study

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:35.820
asks whether a signal shows up in people, often as a biomarker, a scan, or a short safety

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:41.600
check. An outcome trial asks whether fewer people have the events that change a life. Oregon

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:45.900
failure, a hospital stay, death, or a score to find in advance.

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:48.060
Association is not cause.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:51.000
A biomarker that moves is not an outcome.

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:55.400
Stroke research shows the middle rungs are useful and still not final.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:04:01.440
A review in cellular and molecular neurobiology says inflammation and immune processes in

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:06.240
ischemic stroke were shown in vitro and in animal models, and confirmed in people.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:09.020
That is a strong pattern for a methods review.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:14.580
view. The same broad process appears on more than one run. The authors still call translation

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:20.340
into the human disease a hard step, and they say more work has to fill the gaps. Confirming

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:26.200
a process is not a treatment recipe. A paper on damage associated molecular patterns is

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:32.740
not a clinic protocol. Animal prediction fails often enough to have its own review. In biochemical

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:37.900
pharmacology, mechanical and colleagues say animal models have long been used for disease

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:42.820
biology, target finding, and testing new chemical entities in living animals.

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:47.960
Then they describe the criticism after clinical trials failed on compounds that had looked

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:49.420
promising before humans.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:54.720
The limit they name is prediction of efficacy, safety, and toxicity in people.

00:04:55.340 --> 00:04:57.440
Their practical point stays on the latter.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:00.460
Test an idea in more than one disease model.

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:06.780
Measure pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics and build validated biomarkers earlier so

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:12.080
you know the target was engaged. The predictive value of an animal model is only as useful

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:16.720
as the context you read it in. That is the sentence to hold when an ad says,

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:25.060
shown in animals. Biomarkers need the same caution. A 2026 review in lab animal written about tuberculosis

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:31.060
markers across species defines a biomarker as a measurable indicator of a biological state.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:35.880
Those indicators can help diagnosis, prognosis, and watching a treatment.

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:41.580
Clinical studies are limited by cost, ethics, and what you can sample, which is why models

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:42.020
exist.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:45.700
Species differences are both the advantage and the limit.

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:50.720
The review's conclusion is that animal data and human data have to be read together.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:53.660
A marker that moves in a model is a candidate.

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:56.280
It is not yet a diagnosis in a person.

00:05:56.280 --> 00:06:00.500
mechanism work can be precise and still sit below outcomes.

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:06.140
A pharmacotherapy review of vanqulemice and kidney injury describes pre-clinical models

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:11.800
in which the drug builds up in proximal tubule cells, oxidative stress follows, and cells

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:13.200
die by apoptosis.

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:18.640
Injury in those models tracks more with high peak concentrations and the area under the

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:20.380
curve than with trough levels.

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:23.280
That is mechanism, mostly pre-clinical.

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:28.980
The review also says ordinary clinical use still has a poor map of what drives the injury,

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:32.820
and several gaps remain before the drug could be made less toxic.

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:37.500
This spotlight is about seeing that gap, not about vancomycin care.

00:06:38.140 --> 00:06:42.700
What is not established is any universal exchange rate from one rung to the next.

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:47.440
The sleep review does not say a conserved circuit guarantees a human benefit.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:53.780
it. The stroke review does not say human confirmation of inflammation has closed the gap. The animal

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:59.600
model review does not say better biomarkers will save every failed prediction. None of these papers

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:05.880
is a peptide outcome trial, and none of them ranks a named peptide medicine. This is not a compound,

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:13.220
so it has no approval, no label, and no authorized indication. The risk is misreading. A cell result

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:18.840
treated as an animal result, an animal result treated as a human result, or a bio-marker

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:24.640
shift treated as a clinical outcome. Unregulated products add a problem the method cannot fix.

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:29.800
A study of a pure research peptide does not describe the vial in a gray market ad.

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:36.100
Four questions cover most claims. What was studied, in what kind of system, what was measured,

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:40.020
and was that measurement the outcome a person would actually care about?

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:45.380
One thing worth knowing is that a controlled human comparison can flag a nail change in

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:49.480
GLP1 users without proving the cause in any one person.

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:55.400
A human trial that follows lean mass is measuring something a bathroom scale does not, so weight

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:57.800
change and muscle change are separate facts.

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:03.900
A randomized mechanism study in Type 2 diabetes can show how semi-glutide meets kidney tissue

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:06.480
and still not count kidney failure outcomes.

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:12.820
A country-level fall in diabetes prevalence, read with glucose tolerance testing, is surveillance

00:08:12.820 --> 00:08:15.660
of a population, not a verdict on a peptide.

